rem Hopper.tch ----------------- ;
worldelay 1 secs ;
ESC;

win 0 secs no
`Hi! Welcome to the Hopper 4.0 Tutorial. This is a guided tour of Hopper's
 main features. The tutorial lasts about 15 minutes on most computers.
 Press a key only when a tutorial information window is displayed.`;

win 0 secs no
`We will start with the first step which is to go to Treatment. Then we will
 press <Enter> to select Treatment and go to Consult`;

Rem ----------goto treatment ------------;
Left;
Left;

Rem ----------select treatment ------------;
Enter;

Rem ----------select Consult ------------;
C;

win 0 secs no
`We want to create the weather data for Casper, WY. If you were
 selecting here you would want to select the
 town closest to your location.`;

Rem ----------select Create weather file ------------;
Enter;
End;
Up;
Up;
Up;
Up;
Up;
Rem --- Select Casper, WY;
Enter;

win 0 secs no
`Now we will begin the expert system for treatment selection. We could load
 previously saved information from a file.  However, for this example
 we will not load a file, but will enter each item, one at a time.`;
wait 2 secs;
N;
worldelay 2 secs ;
output `070594`;
output `071594`;

Rem Trt date warning is displayed;
Pause;
Enter;

rem ---- early spp;
win 0 secs no
`There is additional help available.  We will briefly look at
 the help information for this variable.`;
F1;
Wait 3 secs;
Pause;
ESC;
output `23`;
Enter;

rem  ---- survey date notice;
Wait 3 secs;
Wait 3 secs;

win 0 secs no
`Here we could change the life stage estimate (also used in the
 Economic Analysis) if it is not similar to field estimates.  For
 now we will accept Hopper's estimate.`;
Enter;

rem ---- Environ Concerns;
Enter;


rem ---- Bees ;
N; Enter;

rem ---- Beneficials;
N; Enter;

rem ---- Environ Sensitive areas;
down; Enter;

rem ---- Density;
down; Enter;

rem ---- Insectaries;
Enter;

rem ---- Thick veg;
Enter;

rem ---- Hot and Dry;
down; Enter;

rem ---- greater than 90%;
down; Enter;

rem WhatIf Screen is displayed;
wait 2 secs;

win 0 secs no
`When the expert system has selected valid treatments, you can modify any of
 your answers by deleting them on the lower screen.  Then the <F5> key
 can be used to start the expert system again and ask you for a new value.`;

win 0 secs no
`Any time the cursor is in the upper screen
 you could press <Escape> to jump to the
 lower screen to make changes, and restart.  If <Escape> is pressed while
 the cursor is in the lower screen, Hopper will exit and return to
 the main menu.`;

rem ---- delete cool and wet;

worldelay 1 secs ;

win 0 secs no
`Now we will delete Cool and Wet.`;
Del;

win 0 secs no
`Now we will delete Closed Canopy and continue with <F5>.`;
down; down; down; down; down; down;
down; down; down;

rem ---- del closed canopy;
Del;


F5;
worldelay 2 secs;

rem Survey date notice;
Pause;
Enter;
rem Thick veg;
Down;
Enter;

rem Hot and dry;
Enter;

rem --- all treatments are shown with WhatIf Screen;
Pause;
win 0 secs
`The list of treatments and input data are acceptable so the Tutorial will
 continue with an <F5>.`;
F5;
N;

win 0 secs
`Hopper will let you view an explanation of the treatment selection
 process.`;

rem Show Explain;
down; Enter; Enter;
wait 3 secs;
wait 3 secs;
wait 3 secs;
rem pause;
rem win 0 secs
`We will exit from the explanation by pressing <Escape>.`;

ESC;
Rem ---- Finish Consult;

win 0 secs
`Now we will go to Economics to determine cost effectiveness of the
 selected treatments.`;
down; Enter;

win 0 secs
`Values from the last Economics run can be used or a different ranch
 model can be loaded.  Here we will load a different ranch model.`;

down; Enter;
win 0 secs no
`A list of available models are presented. There is a description of the models
 in Appendix B of the User Guide. Also, online information is available by
 pressing <F1> for help.  The Tutorial will briefly show you the online
 information.`;

F1;
Pause;
PgDn;
Pause;
PgDn;
pause;
ESC;

win 0 secs no
 `We will select an economics file that was created for the tutorial.`;

rem Jump to the Tutorial ec3 file;
~; Enter;

Enter;
rem delete the line of text;
ctrly;
output `40 site`;
output `calf, North `;
output `Wyoming cow-`;
Enter;
win 0 secs no
`We will enter grasshopper density. This is the only information that
 must be entered. All other information on the screen already
 contains typical values. The Tutorial will enter <F5> to continue to the
 next screen.`;

output `12`;
Enter;
wait 1 secs;
output `20`;
Enter;
wait 3 secs;
F5;

win 0 secs no
`On this screen cost of each treatment should be entered. Cost is one of
 the most important factors in the economic analysis. We will accept these
 typical costs and continue with <F5>.`;
wait 3 secs;
F5;

win 0 secs no
`If the grasshopper populations are expected to remain the same or
 increase there may be multiple years of benefit for treatment. In this
 example we assume no multiple year benefits.`;
rem Y this is not an autoAdvance field;
rem Enter;
rem 1;
wait 3 secs;
F5;

win 0 secs no
`We will accept the typical values on this screen and press <F5> to
 continue.`;
wait 3 secs;
F5;

win 0 secs no
`We will accept the typical values on this screen and press <F5> to
 continue.`;

wait 3 secs;
F5;

win 0 secs no
`We will accept the typical values on this screen and press <F5> to
 continue.`;

wait 3 secs;
F5;
rem Tell user they could save a file here and what info it would contain;
rem win 0 secs no
`The information on the last six screens can be saved and used later. In
 addition, this information is automatically saved as in the LAST file and
 can be used on the very next run.`;
n;
Y;
rem Show plot of No Trt graph;
N;
rem wait 3 secs;
rem pause;
rem Enter;
Enter;
rem Show plot next graph;
N;
rem wait 3 secs;
rem Pause;
rem Enter;
Enter;
rem Show plot of next graph;
N;
rem wait 3 secs;
rem Pause;
rem Enter;
Enter;
rem Show plot of Next graph;
N;
rem wait 3 secs;
rem Pause;
rem Enter;
Enter;
rem Show plot of Next graph;
N;
rem wait 3 secs;
rem Pause;
rem Enter;
Enter;
rem Show plot of Next graph;
N;
rem wait 3 secs;
rem Pause;
rem Enter;
Rem Save results, default = n;
Enter;
enter;
win 0 secs no
`This is the final result screen from the economic analysis. When you
 are finished reading the results press a key to end the tutorial.`;
Enter;
win 0 secs no
`The tutorial is finished.`;
EndScript;
rem ------------------------------------------ done;
